      "title": "Models",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "version": "7.5.2",
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Main Model\n\nKrea 2 RAW.\n\n[Bf16 & FP8 versions](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/diffusion_models)\n\n[GGUF versions](https://huggingface.co/vantagewithai/Krea-2-Raw-GGUF/tree/main)\n\nThe RAW model is recommended, but for this workflow you can use the turbo model if you want.\n\nGoes in models/diffusion_models\n\n## Turbo Lora\n\n[Rank 64 Turbo Lora](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/blob/main/loras/krea2_turbo_lora_rank_64_bf16.safetensors)\n\nRequired when using the RAW model. Set it to 1.0 strength for this workflow.\n\nGoes in models/loras\n\n## Anti-Censorship Lora\n\n[2 Vector Bypass Lora](https://civitai.com/models/2728234/krea2filterbypass?modelVersionId=3066812)\n\nRequired if you want the model to work properly, even for SFW prompts. Set it to only 1.0 strength most of the time, but sometimes you may need to set it higher (2-6) if the model keeps refusing to do what you ask. This is a thing even for SFW prompts, especially when you want strong facial expressions.\n\nGoes in models/loras\n\n## Text Encoder\n\n[Qwen 3 VL 4B](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/text_encoders)\n\nUse BF16 if you can.\n\nGoes in models/text_encoders\n\n## VAE\n\n[Wan 2.1 FP32 VAE (RECOMMENDED)](https://huggingface.co/Kijai/WanVideo_comfy/blob/main/Wan2_1_VAE_fp32.safetensors)\n\nThe FP32 Wan VAE gives sharp results and has no downsides.\n\n\n[Wan 2.1 Upscale2x VAE (OPTIONAL)](https://huggingface.co/spacepxl/Wan2.1-VAE-upscale2x/blob/main/Wan2.1_VAE_upscale2x_imageonly_real_v1.safetensors)\n\nThis gives even sharper results than the regular Wan 2.1 FP32 VAE, but it also introduces noise & artifacts to the image.\n\nTo use it, you need the VAE-Utils Comfy node set installed so you can use the 'VAE Decode (VAE Utils)' node instead of the normal vae decoder. You also need to downscale your image by 0.5 afterwards (the VAE doubles the resolution).\n\n[Qwen Image VAE (OPTIONAL)](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/vae)\n\nThe qwen image VAE is the 'normal' one for Krea 2. It gives blurrier results than the Wan 2.1 FP32 VAE, but you may prefer it this way if you plan to post-process your images.\n\nGoes in models/vae"
      ],
      "color": "#2a363b",
      "bgcolor": "#3f5159"
    }
